Power System Protection — S. A. Soman, IIT Bombay (@pe-nptel-protection: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_52Z22QR7WGDJHAFBDMPFGYCXJE
S. A. Soman. [Complete NPTEL Power System Protection course, 108101039](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/108101039).

Work all forty lectures and tutorials: protection principles, instrument transformers and saturation, sequence/fault models, overcurrent/fuse and earth-fault protection, directional and distance schemes, power swings/out-of-step behavior, sampled phasor/DSP methods, and bus/transformer/generator differential protection. Reconstruct numerical settings and test them against alternative operating/fault cases rather than memorizing one example.

The official course index identifies the instructor, institution and module/lecture sequence; checked on 29 October 2026. Public learning access, registration/certification and permission to reuse media are distinct. No blanket licence for every embedded figure or referenced standard is inferred from an open course page. The course's physical principles remain useful while actual equipment data, accepted practices and applicable requirements must be checked for the intended installation. No videos, notes or relay files are bundled.

**Return:** [Power-engineering sources — complete books, courses, methods and evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_12EFX00X7ZXGT9MPMJDYRTNY9N).
